    "title": "'Go Now' evacuation orders issued for some in Rainier, Thurston County due to wildfire - NewsBreak",
    "text": "Level 3 ‘Leave Now’ evacuation orders have been issued for people in Rainier, a city in Thurston County, for a wildfire. Those who live in the area of Rainier Road between 138th Ave SE and Military Road are told to leave. For those on the outskirts of that area, a Level 2 “get ready” evaucation order was issued. The Level 2 order is in effect for people east of Rainier Road to Rainier Acres Road, and south of 128th Ave S. South of 138th Ave. SE to Finian Road are also under this order. It’s unclear how big the fire is. The order went into effect at 4:20 p.m. Roads may be blocked or congested, so plan your route accordingly. Tenino High School has opened as a shelter location (500 W 2nd Avenue). This is a developing story. KIRO 7 will continue to track updates as they come in.",
